Z||000000||JSocha||07-11-2001||12:58 AM||||I'm running Norton AntiVirus against my emails that now come in because of an earlier virus that was passed from our purchasing department at work.<P>Today, Fiero Digest Request #646 was detected by NAV as containing the WScript.KakWorm.<P>It comes in on the following email attachement labeled NAE17.MME & NAE3D.MME.<P>More information can be found on this virus if needed at:  <A HREF="http://www.sarc.com/avcenter/venc/data/wscript.kakworm.htr" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sarc.com/avcenter/venc/data/wscript.kakworm.htr</A> <P>So, if you have a subscription and are polifierated with email from Fiero Digest Request at Fiero.org, this is just a heads up, especially if you do not have a virus detection program enabled on your end.<P>Went right through my ISP which typically defangs them through their virus detection software if detected.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||JSocha||07-11-2001||10:49 AM||||I have got to learn how to type at night, especially in this dark room.<P>Should have been Fiero Digest #696 not #646.<P>Didn't notice it until this morning when I looked and said to myself..."That's not right!".<P>Damn fingers.  Bad Fingers! Bad! Bad! Bad Fingers!||||reg||1
